<heading>list - List exits from a box.</heading>

<rule/>

<heading level="2">
Usage
</heading>

<pre>
  list --world NAME
  list --world NAME --box NAME
</pre>

<heading level="2">
Description
</heading>

<paragraph>
Lists all exits from a box, or all exits in a world when
no box is specified.
</paragraph>

<paragraph>
An exit is an endpoint: the local view of a connection as
seen from its box. It has a name, an orientation (angle from
the room's own frame) and leads to another box.
</paragraph>

<heading level="2">
Examples
</heading>

<pre>
list --world Work --box Office
  List exits from the Office box.

list --world Work
  List all exits in the Work world.

exit/list --world Research --box Lab
  From another space, qualify the path.
</pre>

<heading level="2">
See also
</heading>

<paragraph>
delete, edit, show
</paragraph>
